\ Stage 3 read-only ATA PIO driver, implemented in Franc.
\ Target: legacy primary-master IDE under QEMU. Never writes a sector.
\ Values: lba ata-read-sector -> 1 success, 0 unavailable/timeout/error.
\ Read 512 bytes into sector-buffer using byte writes. The older C disk store
\ still handles persistent writes until an independent Franc driver is tested.
\ No IRQs; the hardware-facing substrate is io8@, io8!, io16@ and memory !.
def at-wait :at-count 0 :at-i begin at-i at-count - while $1F7 io8@ :at-status at-status $FF - if0 0 exit then at-status 128 band if0 at-status 33 band ifnz 0 exit then at-status 8 band ifnz 1 exit then then at-i 1 + :at-i repeat 0 ;
def ata-read-sector :at-lba hardware? if0 0 exit then at-lba 0 - if 0 exit then at-lba 256 - if 1 else 0 exit then :at-bounds 200000 at-wait drop $1F6 $E0 at-lba 16777216 / floor 15 band + io8! $1F2 1 io8! $1F3 at-lba 255 band io8! $1F4 at-lba 256 / floor 255 band io8! $1F5 at-lba 65536 / floor 255 band io8! $1F7 $20 io8! 200000 at-wait if0 0 exit then 0 :at-i begin at-i 256 - while $1F0 io16@ :at-word at-i 2 * at-word 255 band sector-byte! at-i 2 * 1 + at-word 256 / floor sector-byte! at-i 1 + :at-i repeat 1 ;
\ Probe the first byte of FRANCFS1 at LBA 128; expected ASCII F (70).
def ata-header-byte 128 ata-read-sector if0 0 exit then 0 sector-byte@ ;
